WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:36.830
<b>28 Years Ago

Second Year
of Oden's Voyage</b>

3
00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:34.030
28 years ago,

4
00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:37.120
during the second year
of Oden's journey.

5
00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:41.500
<b>Roger and Whitebeard</b>

6
00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:41.540
My son is born!

7
00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:42.580
Name him Egg!

8
00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:43.540
Seaweed!

9
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:44.540
Fishcake!

10
00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:46.170
Meatball!

11
00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:50.050
Stop! I am not naming him
after things you put in oden!

12
00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:52.090
Our son is peerless among men!

13
00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:55.320
Therefore his name
must reflect that!

14
00:01:56.140 --> 00:02:00.540
He shall be known as
Kozuki Momonosuke!

15
00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:05.940
I'll remind you,
you're a wanted man now.

16
00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:07.190
So outside of Wano,

17
00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:09.440
you're just another
criminal with a bounty.

18
00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.700
If you truly care about
Lady Toki and Lord Momonosuke,

19
00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:15.700
why don't you consider returning
home, where they can be safe?

20
00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:17.120
I am not ready yet.

21
00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.200
There is still an answer
I'm searching for.

22
00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.660
Please, don't worry.
We're all right.

23
00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:22.910
We have strong friends.

24
00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:25.250
Still, it's a pity that
these newspaper things

25
00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:28.540
don't give us any updates on
what's happening back in Wano.

26
00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:30.210
How could they,

27
00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:32.300
since no information
ever leaves the country?

28
00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:34.050
It's just like Zou.

29
00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:36.840
I wonder how
the other retainers are.

30
00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:45.510
Eh? Divisions, in the crew?

31
00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:47.470
There's quite a few of us.

32
00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:51.900
So. I think five divisions
should work out fine.

33
00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:54.690
Great idea, Pops. I like it.

34
00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:57.150
Oh! Let me be
a commander, please?

35
00:02:57.190 --> 00:02:58.150
Me, too!

36
00:02:58.150 --> 00:02:59.150
Oden!

37
00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:02.490
You will serve as the
second division commander.

38
00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:07.870
I, uh, well,
I'm not sure that I would...

39
00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:10.620
Do it!

40
00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:13.710
Just as fate
brought us to Whitebeard,

41
00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:16.000
so did it bring
other crewmembers.

42
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:20.050
Listen, we're not fisherman
or merchants, we're pirates!

43
00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:22.260
I don't care! Please!

44
00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:24.140
I've got nowhere else to go!

45
00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:26.260
Hey! Stop!

46
00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:28.520
What's your name, kid?

47
00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.180
It's, uh, Teach, sir.

48
00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:38.630
Fine then. Come aboard!

49
00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:42.720
Thank you so much, sir!

50
00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:47.390
Another orphan, it seems.

51
00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:50.520
Did you see that?

52
00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:52.220
Something's flying over there!

53
00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:58.070
No matter how far
we sail, I desire to see more.

54
00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:01.650
Commander,
wait! We have to scout first!

55
00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:04.610
I don't know how
to end an adventure like this

56
00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.530
once it's begun!

57
00:04:08.590 --> 00:04:11.970
Meanwhile, in the Land of Wano.

58
00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:12.570
Special report! Special report!

59
00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:16.620
Terrible news!
Lord Sukiyaki is critically ill!

60
00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:18.830
His end may be close at hand!

61
00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:20.080
Shogun, no!

62
00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:23.080
The country
faced a serious cris.

63
00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:26.750
And so, the daimyos from each
region in the Land of Wano

64
00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:29.800
came to the Flower Capital
to meet with the shogun.

65
00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:35.260
I want Oden to succeed me.

66
00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:35.340
He must become the next shogun.

67
00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:37.600
He must be the next shogun.

68
00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:40.470
Of course, my lord.
Just as you wish.

69
00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:43.220
However,
since Oden is not here with us,

70
00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:45.680
However, since Oden is not here,

71
00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:45.940
I must assign a proxy
to take his place,

72
00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:49.230
I must assign a proxy to take
his place for the time being.

73
00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:51.610
I fear that before he returns,

74
00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:55.450
something unfortunate
may befall me.

75
00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:57.380
I have chosen this man,

76
00:04:57.380 --> 00:04:58.450
I have chosen the man Oden
treated like a little brother.

77
00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:01.290
who Oden treated
like a little brother.

78
00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:02.660
Kurozumi Orochi!

79
00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:06.250
His name is Kurozumi Orochi.

80
00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:06.510
Orochi? What's going on here?

81
00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:10.730
Orochi? What is this?

82
00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:12.300
Oden "treated him
like a brother," he says?

83
00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:17.010
Oden treated him
like a brother, he says. Really?

84
00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:19.790
I am grateful.

85
00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:22.790
You have given me an opportunity
to clear the Kurozumi name!

86
00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:25.500
I owe a great debt to
Lord Sukiyaki for this.

87
00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:28.460
And to Lord Oden,
for his kindness.

88
00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:31.420
I will atone for
my grandfather's mistakes,

89
00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:32.760
as best I can.

90
00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:36.180
I shall humbly prepare
the throne for Lord Oden,

91
00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:38.510
so that he may ascend someday.

92
00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:43.510
I will be
but a puppet upon that seat,

93
00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:45.890
awaiting Lord Oden's return.

94
00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:49.980
So I beg for your aid and
your guidance until then.

95
00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:54.510
You're a Kurozumi, are you?
Why didn't you tell me?

96
00:05:54.510 --> 00:05:56.930
So sorry!

97
00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:03.900
sorry.

98
00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:18.580
I can see the future!

99
00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:21.160
I see you!

100
00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:29.590
You will become the shogun!

101
00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:38.260
You're out of your mind, lady!
Tell me who you are right now!

102
00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:44.180
Your grandfather.
Do you know how he died?

103
00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:48.150
Well,
I don't know the details, but...

104
00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:49.900
I was told he committed seppuku?

105
00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:53.320
A lie! He was killed
by the Kozukis!

106
00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:56.030
What? But he committed
some kind of crime, right?

107
00:06:56.030 --> 00:07:00.240
It was a struggle
for political power!

108
00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:02.660
A struggle for power?

109
00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:05.870
Whoever stands at
the top writes the rules!

110
00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:09.040
His actions were only called
a "crime" because he lost!

111
00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:13.130
The previous Kozuki shogun
had a weakness, you see!

112
00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:16.010
Try as he might,
he couldn't sire a child!

113
00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:18.220
He had no heir!

114
00:07:18.220 --> 00:07:21.140
This bred uncertainty
among the five daimyos

115
00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:23.430
serving under the Kozuki Clan.

116
00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:29.180
<b>Shimotsuki
Clan</b>

117
00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:26.890
Suddenly, it was unclear
who would be the next shogun.

118
00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:29.180
<b>Kurozumi
Clan</b>

119
00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:29.180
<b>Uzuki
Clan</b>

120
00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:29.180
<b>Amatsuki
Clan</b>

121
00:07:26.890 --> 00:07:29.900
"Why, it should be me!"
they all thought!

122
00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:29.180
<b>Fugetsu
Clan</b>

123
00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:32.230
But your grandfather
did more than think!

124
00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:34.230
He was making preparations.

125
00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:36.150
And by "making preparations,"

126
00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:39.990
I mean he was poisoning those
rival daimyos one by one!

127
00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:42.330
He made it look like
an inside job,

128
00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:45.240
as if each region had
its own struggle for power.

129
00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:47.250
The shogun, wracked with grief

130
00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:52.210
over the deaths of his loyal
daimyos, eventually fell ill!

131
00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:54.920
Everything was going
according to plan.

132
00:07:54.920 --> 00:07:56.800
But just when it seemed
that his ambitions

133
00:07:56.800 --> 00:08:00.550
would be realized,
disaster struck!

134
00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:05.450
The shogun got what
he needed at last.

135
00:08:05.450 --> 00:08:08.710
An heir: Kozuki Sukiyaki!

136
00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:11.380
A miracle!

137
00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:17.720
Curse you, Sukiyaki!

138
00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:21.970
Oh, your grandfather
was so close!

139
00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:24.970
But not only was his plan
thwarted, it was exposed!

140
00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:26.350
He was brought low!

141
00:08:26.350 --> 00:08:28.520
They forced him
to commit seppuku!

142
00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:30.900
Then the clan lost everything!

143
00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:34.860
Their territory, property,
and power were stolen!

144
00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:37.900
People despised
the name "Kurozumi"!

145
00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:41.530
The clan was tossed in the
streets, made lower than dirt!

146
00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:43.910
Tell me, whose fault is that?

147
00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:48.910
Who is to blame for
your misery and poverty?

148
00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:52.210
Not your grandfather, who wanted
the best for his family!

149
00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:55.230
When did it all go wrong?

150
00:08:55.230 --> 00:09:00.780
When he was born!
Kozuki Sukiyaki!

151
00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:05.070
That's right!
If he was never born,

152
00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:09.280
you surely would have
become the shogun someday!

153
00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:14.290
Shogun Orochi! I love you!

154
00:09:14.290 --> 00:09:17.660
Yes, we all do!
You're just the best!

155
00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:20.800
Oh, Shogun!

156
00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:25.010
You're too much, girls!

157
00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:27.640
Really? Shogun?

158
00:09:27.640 --> 00:09:32.020
But of course!
Oh, it's just galling, isn't it?

159
00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:36.400
Wait, don't tell me
you're like me?

160
00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:39.690
Is that why you care?
Because you're a Kurozumi, too?

161
00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:41.820
Who I am is of
no importance anymore,

162
00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:43.490
don't you understand?

163
00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:45.400
I was out of the
country for years,

164
00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:47.910
it's been a terrible ordeal.

165
00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:51.290
Now, watch very closely.

166
00:09:56.060 --> 00:09:58.480
You stole my face!

167
00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:01.890
What you've just witnessed is

168
00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:04.440
the power of the
Clone-Clone Fruit.

169
00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:08.190
And there's more
where that came from!

170
00:10:08.190 --> 00:10:11.410
Do as I bid,
and I'll give you power, too!

171
00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:12.150
I'll

172
00:10:12.150 --> 00:10:14.930
The power you need
to become shogun!

173
00:10:14.930 --> 00:10:18.140
I'll do whatever
you want! Tell me!

174
00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:23.960
The first step is to raise money
and produce weapons.

175
00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:27.380
The craftsmen in the Land
of Wano possess great skill!

176
00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:30.590
Using weapons as leverage,
you can gain powerful backers

177
00:10:30.590 --> 00:10:33.260
from across the seas!

178
00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:35.100
I understand!

179
00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:51.510
<b>Hakumai</b>

180
00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:51.510
My name is Orochi.

181
00:10:51.510 --> 00:10:54.340
I'll accept any work
that you can provide!

182
00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:56.220
My entire family has fallen ill,

183
00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:59.390
so if I don't work,
I fear that they'll all starve!

184
00:10:59.390 --> 00:11:03.940
I see. You have my sympathy.
We'll work something out.

185
00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:07.940
<b>A Month

Later</b>

186
00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:07.870
Lord Yasuie!

187
00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:10.630
What's that? You said
Orochi disappeared?

188
00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:15.760
Yes. Also, I don't know
if it's a coincidence or not,

189
00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:18.220
but it appears your safe
has been emptied out.

190
00:11:18.220 --> 00:11:22.260
What? The money is gone, too?

191
00:11:23.250 --> 00:11:26.210
<b>Kuri</b>

192
00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:28.980
Didn't I met you at Yasu's
place a while back?

193
00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:30.920
Yes, yes. The name is Orochi.

194
00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:34.130
Lord Yasuie has already
helped me so much.

195
00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:37.300
I could never borrow
money from him!

196
00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:39.470
Fair enough.
You can count on me!

197
00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:42.060
– Lord, wait!
– Thank you so much, sir!

198
00:11:44.980 --> 00:11:46.480
I need money!

199
00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:48.560
Again?

200
00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:49.940
I need money!

201
00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:51.480
Again?

202
00:11:54.070 --> 00:11:56.320
Please lend me money!

203
00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:59.780
I can pay you back for sure
this time, you have my word!

204
00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:01.240
I beg of you!

205
00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:05.040
My Lord Oden!

206
00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:07.670
I'll remind you,
our own finances are not

207
00:12:07.710 --> 00:12:09.840
exactly in immaculate shape!

208
00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:12.300
But he said that
he'd pay it back, right?

209
00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:14.260
<b>Flower

Capital</b>

210
00:12:14.260 --> 00:12:18.970
<b>Kozuki Sukiyaki

(Oden's Father)

Shogun of Wano</b>

211
00:12:15.140 --> 00:12:17.930
Oden. You've come
with no retainers?

212
00:12:17.930 --> 00:12:19.480
Why are you here?

213
00:12:18.890 --> 00:12:21.560
Could you please let this
fellow stay here a while?

214
00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:24.310
He works hard, and he's
good at preparing medicine.

215
00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:27.320
He is like
a little brother to me.

216
00:12:27.320 --> 00:12:30.480
My name is Orochi.

217
00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:35.670
Everyone, take good care
of Orochi for me!

218
00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:37.840
As you wish, my lord.

219
00:12:47.810 --> 00:12:50.140
The Shogun Sukiyaki!

220
00:12:50.140 --> 00:12:54.480
I've done it! I've clawed
my way up to the top!

221
00:12:54.300 --> 00:13:00.260
<b>Back to

Where We

Started</b>

222
00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:09.080
Stay with us, Lord Sukiyaki,
you must be strong!

223
00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:10.410
Hang on, please!

224
00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:11.830
We're here with you!

225
00:13:11.830 --> 00:13:16.090
If I cannot
overcome this illness,

226
00:13:16.090 --> 00:13:17.760
carry on in my place!

227
00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:23.260
Certainly! I'll do my best!

228
00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:25.640
Orochi will need your help.

229
00:13:25.640 --> 00:13:28.350
I ask that you support him
as best you can.

230
00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:29.480
Yes.

231
00:13:29.480 --> 00:13:30.640
– Lord Sukiyaki!

232
00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:32.140
We'd better get you a doctor.

233
00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:33.940
We'll be back shortly!

234
00:13:33.940 --> 00:13:35.980
Help! We need a physician!

235
00:13:37.110 --> 00:13:39.400
Lord Sukiyaki!
Please don't leave us!

236
00:13:39.400 --> 00:13:40.690
We need you!

237
00:13:40.690 --> 00:13:43.070
I leave this land
in your hands, Orochi!

238
00:13:43.070 --> 00:13:46.660
It's far too early to say
such a thing, my lord!

239
00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:57.880
I said you'd become
the shogun, didn't I?

240
00:14:02.630 --> 00:14:05.890
The Land of Wano
was seized with great sadness

241
00:14:05.890 --> 00:14:10.850
as news of Shogun Sukiyaki's
death spread across the country.

242
00:14:21.270 --> 00:14:24.940
One day, in the
fourth year of Oden's journey.

243
00:14:25.820 --> 00:14:27.400
Look at that!

244
00:14:27.400 --> 00:14:30.360
Whoa! They're going crazy!

245
00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:31.620
What happened?

246
00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:34.200
I've never seen fish
act like this before!

247
00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:37.040
You think
a natural disaster is coming?

248
00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:43.590
It seems like they're all
headed away from that island.

249
00:14:43.590 --> 00:14:45.340
You're right.

250
00:14:45.340 --> 00:14:48.380
Bet some kinda giant
monster lives there!

251
00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:50.220
Marco! Go check it out!

252
00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:53.390
What, and spoil the surprise?
No thank you!

253
00:15:01.810 --> 00:15:05.520
I'll protect you,
and your big brother!

254
00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:07.650
We're gonna go, aren't we?

255
00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:10.780
'Course we are.

256
00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:16.370
You ready?

257
00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:18.830
Yeah!

258
00:15:33.430 --> 00:15:35.850
What's going on here?

259
00:15:35.850 --> 00:15:39.430
Even the tough-lookin'
animals are runnin' away!

260
00:15:39.430 --> 00:15:42.600
Something is out there.
Something strong.

261
00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:50.110
If you guys wanna
catch me that bad,

262
00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:52.820
y'better bring Garp
or Sengoku next time.

263
00:15:54.070 --> 00:15:57.030
Fighting you is no sport at all.

264
00:15:57.740 --> 00:16:01.550
Captain! Whitebeard's
ship just showed up!

265
00:16:01.550 --> 00:16:03.340
I think they know we're here!

266
00:16:03.340 --> 00:16:05.630
Looks like they're on
the other side of the island!

267
00:16:05.630 --> 00:16:09.340
We just finished one fight,
Roger. What now?

268
00:16:09.880 --> 00:16:11.220
Whitebeard, huh?

269
00:16:11.220 --> 00:16:13.550
Haven't seen him
in quite a while.

270
00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:18.970
If the birds are taking off,

271
00:16:18.970 --> 00:16:21.020
he must've come ashore.

272
00:16:21.020 --> 00:16:21.140
All right!
Let's have a bout, then!

273
00:16:21.140 --> 00:16:24.650
All right!
Let's have a bout then!

274
00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:27.480
You can only risk death
while you're still alive!

275
00:16:28.860 --> 00:16:31.610
My end is coming soon,
after all!

276
00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:31.620
Odds are this is the last time
you and I will ever cross paths.

277
00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:35.750
Odds are, this is the last time
you and I will ever cross paths.

278
00:16:35.750 --> 00:16:37.320
Whitebeard.

279
00:16:37.320 --> 00:16:40.120
There's some weird guy in robes
who's running crazy fast!

280
00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:41.540
A samurai!

281
00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:44.920
He's here, too, huh? Lucky me!

282
00:16:47.380 --> 00:16:49.460
All of you are running too slow!

283
00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:51.000
I think you're
too fast, actually!

284
00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:53.510
I'm supposed to plunder
their treasure first, right?

285
00:16:53.510 --> 00:16:55.800
This is totally different
than our usual battles!

286
00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:58.800
The Roger Pirates
are seriously tough!

287
00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:01.100
He's not listening at all!

288
00:17:19.910 --> 00:17:23.080
Gun Modoki!

289
00:17:34.340 --> 00:17:36.420
He's as strong
as they say he is.

290
00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:38.840
I think he's wreaked
enough havoc for now.

291
00:17:38.840 --> 00:17:39.890
I agree.

292
00:17:39.890 --> 00:17:42.680
Gaban! Rayleigh! Wait!

293
00:17:42.680 --> 00:17:46.360
Allow me. I'd sure hate
to see my crew get hurt!

294
00:17:47.480 --> 00:17:49.730
You just wanna fight him.

295
00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:55.660
I smell a beast!

296
00:17:55.660 --> 00:17:58.570
Ahoy there, samurai!

297
00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:02.180
Divine Departure!

298
00:18:24.470 --> 00:18:27.000
What in the hell was that?

299
00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:33.860
Listen up, pal.
We can't have that.

300
00:18:44.780 --> 00:18:46.790
There you are!

301
00:19:26.450 --> 00:19:30.450
You're looking well, Roger!
Good to see you!

302
00:19:30.450 --> 00:19:33.290
How many years
has it been, Newgate?

303
00:19:33.290 --> 00:19:36.250
Too many, I say!

304
00:19:51.070 --> 00:19:53.410
– Now hand over all you've got.
– Now hand over all you've got.

305
00:19:53.410 --> 00:19:54.410
Mess 'em up!

306
00:19:55.830 --> 00:19:56.910
Let's go!

307
00:19:58.290 --> 00:19:59.500
It was a clash between

308
00:19:59.500 --> 00:20:02.120
the greatest crews of the age.

309
00:20:07.920 --> 00:20:11.300
The Roger Pirates
versus the Whitebeard Pirates.

310
00:20:11.400 --> 00:20:12.860
<b>Second Day</b>

311
00:20:11.680 --> 00:20:15.890
The intense battle lasted for
three days and three nights.

312
00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:20.390
Time to get serious!

313
00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:26.610
Sorry, kid, but I'm
always serious. Tough break.

314
00:20:36.720 --> 00:20:38.720
<b>Third Day</b>

315
00:20:52.880 --> 00:20:54.380
Cheers!

316
00:20:54.380 --> 00:20:56.800
How's three boxes
of jerky for one barrel?

317
00:20:54.520 --> 00:21:04.450
<b>Fourth Day...</b>

318
00:20:56.800 --> 00:20:58.100
Good deal!

319
00:20:58.100 --> 00:21:01.060
I like this shirt!
Where did you find this one?

320
00:21:01.060 --> 00:21:02.560
Let me have more!

321
00:21:02.560 --> 00:21:04.400
Hold it! You took too much!

322
00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:07.480
It's gotta be an
even exchange, buddy!

323
00:21:07.480 --> 00:21:08.940
All right, fine.

324
00:21:08.940 --> 00:21:11.150
Got something else
to fork over, then?

325
00:21:11.150 --> 00:21:12.900
You betcha!

326
00:21:12.900 --> 00:21:16.530
Looks like the pillaging
has become a gift exchange.

327
00:21:20.330 --> 00:21:22.620
Who are those two, apprentices?

328
00:21:22.620 --> 00:21:25.500
Hm? Ahh.

329
00:21:25.500 --> 00:21:28.630
Yeah, they have been
tagging along for a while now.

330
00:21:28.630 --> 00:21:31.000
Kinda puny if you ask me.

331
00:21:32.050 --> 00:21:33.720
But look at those faces.

332
00:21:33.720 --> 00:21:36.050
They look like
hardened old vets.

333
00:21:36.800 --> 00:21:39.470
Shanks! Look over there!

334
00:21:39.470 --> 00:21:39.530
What is it?

335
00:21:39.530 --> 00:21:41.280
Do you see that guy?

336
00:21:41.620 --> 00:21:44.250
The mean lookin' one
with the dumb lid.

337
00:21:44.250 --> 00:21:45.960
Yeah?

338
00:21:45.960 --> 00:21:48.420
I heard he didn't sleep
during the ceasefire last night,

339
00:21:48.420 --> 00:21:50.540
or the night before, either!

340
00:21:50.540 --> 00:21:54.050
Hm? Yeah, so?
Prolly just showing off.

341
00:21:54.050 --> 00:21:56.760
Are you stupid? It's not normal!

342
00:21:56.760 --> 00:21:59.470
From what I hear, he's never
slept a day in his life!

343
00:21:59.470 --> 00:22:02.060
Huh? Didn't know
people could do that.

344
00:22:02.060 --> 00:22:06.100
Wow, cool! He must get
to have double the fun!

345
00:22:06.100 --> 00:22:07.480
"Fun," he says!

346
00:22:07.480 --> 00:22:10.100
Yeah, that guy looks
like a barrel of laughs.

347
00:22:10.100 --> 00:22:12.560
He's a monster!

348
00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:13.690
You think?

349
00:22:15.320 --> 00:22:17.700
So. Oden!

350
00:22:17.700 --> 00:22:20.240
Can you make
any sense of this text?

351
00:22:20.780 --> 00:22:23.030
Indeed, I can read it.

352
00:22:23.030 --> 00:22:26.290
But you must tell me why
you possess this script!

353
00:22:26.290 --> 00:22:27.910
Knowledge of these
writings has been

354
00:22:27.910 --> 00:22:30.500
passed down from
generation to generation,

355
00:22:30.500 --> 00:22:33.220
exclusively in the Kozuki Clan.

356
00:22:33.220 --> 00:22:36.390
It all started 13 years ago.

357
00:22:37.520 --> 00:22:40.520
We landed at the destination
of the final Log Pose,

358
00:22:40.520 --> 00:22:44.860
and arrived at a place no man
had ever set foot upon before.

359
00:22:42.340 --> 00:22:46.590
<b>Lodestar Island</b>

360
00:22:44.860 --> 00:22:46.860
Lodestar Island!

361
00:22:46.860 --> 00:22:49.660
We disembarked with a smile,

362
00:22:49.660 --> 00:22:51.740
but our victory
was an empty one.

363
00:22:51.740 --> 00:22:54.700
'Cause we learned that it
wasn't the final island!

364
00:22:55.040 --> 00:22:57.870
The Log Pose needles were
spinning out of control,

365
00:22:57.870 --> 00:23:00.120
refusing to guide us further!

366
00:23:00.120 --> 00:23:02.630
That's when it dawned on me.

367
00:23:02.630 --> 00:23:05.170
There was one last destination!

368
00:23:05.170 --> 00:23:06.800
And once I visit there,

369
00:23:06.800 --> 00:23:08.840
I will be the first
person to travel

370
00:23:08.840 --> 00:23:11.890
the entirety of the world!

371
00:23:12.260 --> 00:23:13.300
Look at this.

372
00:23:13.300 --> 00:23:15.600
These letters will
show me the way!

373
00:23:15.600 --> 00:23:17.560
They're rubbings that
my crew and I took

374
00:23:17.560 --> 00:23:19.520
from a huge red stone!

375
00:23:19.980 --> 00:23:21.770
There are four of
those stones out there

376
00:23:21.770 --> 00:23:23.610
and the World Government
has always

377
00:23:23.610 --> 00:23:26.480
forbidden anyone
from deciphering them.

378
00:23:26.480 --> 00:23:29.280
They're called
Poneglyphs, y'see.

379
00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:34.390
<b>Lodestar Island</b>

380
00:23:30.280 --> 00:23:32.820
I assumed they were
just cultural relics,

381
00:23:32.820 --> 00:23:35.490
but as it turns out,
they're part of a map

382
00:23:34.390 --> 00:23:36.890
<b>Lodestar Island</b>

383
00:23:35.490 --> 00:23:40.120
that reveals the location of
the last, legendary island!

384
00:23:41.790 --> 00:23:41.940
Seems odd the
Government prohibits us

385
00:23:41.940 --> 00:23:43.710
Seems odd
the Government prohibits us

386
00:23:43.710 --> 00:23:43.820
from looking into it!

387
00:23:43.820 --> 00:23:45.300
from looking into it, huh?

388
00:23:45.300 --> 00:23:45.990
There must be
a vast treasure there!

389
00:23:45.990 --> 00:23:47.720
There must be a
vast treasure there!

390
00:23:47.720 --> 00:23:50.760
How could I possibly resist?

391
00:23:50.760 --> 00:23:52.550
The crew who
finds it will become

392
00:23:52.550 --> 00:23:54.850
the greatest pirates
in the world!

393
00:23:54.850 --> 00:23:59.230
So, let's get out there,
shall we?

394
00:24:03.860 --> 00:24:05.470
The greatest?

395
00:24:05.470 --> 00:24:09.930
So, then! We've got
a lot to discuss, don't we?

396
00:24:29.490 --> 00:24:31.870
I was frozen stiff.

397
00:24:31.870 --> 00:24:35.580
For the second time that day,
I found myself stunned.

398
00:24:35.920 --> 00:24:38.460
Who was this fellow?

399
00:24:46.510 --> 00:24:48.890
Believing in old
fairy tales now?

400
00:24:48.890 --> 00:24:51.390
You sound like a child, Roger!

401
00:24:57.390 --> 00:25:00.360
But I'm being completely
serious here, Newgate!

402
00:25:01.520 --> 00:25:02.290
Please! Just for one year,

403
00:25:02.290 --> 00:25:03.350
Please!

404
00:25:03.350 --> 00:25:05.320
Just for one year,
allow me to borrow Oden!

405
00:25:05.320 --> 00:25:07.710
allow me to borrow Oden!

406
00:25:07.710 --> 00:25:11.260
It's all that I'm asking!
I need that man!

407
00:25:11.260 --> 00:25:15.240
With him, I can find
the last island!

408
00:25:15.240 --> 00:25:19.120
Hey! Don't I get
a say in any of this?

409
00:25:19.120 --> 00:25:21.080
Please, Newgate.

410
00:25:23.340 --> 00:25:24.960
I am begging you!

411
00:25:24.960 --> 00:25:26.720
Captain! What're you doing?

412
00:25:26.720 --> 00:25:29.760
Get on your feet!
He's our enemy!

413
00:25:31.600 --> 00:25:33.850
Why would you bow
your head like that?

414
00:25:33.850 --> 00:25:36.020
Have a bit of dignity, man!

415
00:25:36.350 --> 00:25:40.100
I need you, Oden!
You must join us!

416
00:25:40.100 --> 00:25:42.360
I only ask for
a year of your time!

417
00:25:44.050 --> 00:25:47.820
I forbid it!

418
00:25:48.950 --> 00:25:49.220
Roger! Are you trying to
steal my family away from me?

419
00:25:49.220 --> 00:25:52.930
Roger! Are you trying to steal
my family away from me?

420
00:25:53.410 --> 00:25:57.450
I felt a bolt of
excitement shoot down my spine.

421
00:25:57.750 --> 00:26:01.250
Why is it that only the Kozuki
can read those letters?

422
00:26:01.790 --> 00:26:05.380
Was it fate that brought me
together with this man?

423
00:26:12.220 --> 00:26:12.960
Before I knew it,
the words were leaving

424
00:26:12.960 --> 00:26:14.760
I forbid it!

425
00:26:14.760 --> 00:26:17.310
my mouth without restraint!

426
00:26:17.310 --> 00:26:17.450
Please, White-kichi!
I want to go!

427
00:26:17.450 --> 00:26:21.140
Please, White-Kichi!
I want to go!

428
00:26:21.140 --> 00:26:23.590
Will you please permit me?

429
00:26:23.590 --> 00:26:27.780
It would be a dream to see
the last island for myself!

430
00:26:31.610 --> 00:26:33.160
He's annoyed!

431
00:26:33.160 --> 00:26:35.740
Of course I'm annoyed,
you idiot!

432
00:26:35.740 --> 00:26:38.740
How could you do this?
We're practically like brothers!

433
00:26:38.740 --> 00:26:41.620
It will only be
a year, White-kichi!

434
00:26:49.800 --> 00:26:51.760
I beg you!

435
00:26:55.660 --> 00:26:57.490
You better take care
of yourself!

436
00:26:57.490 --> 00:26:58.910
I shall.

437
00:26:59.280 --> 00:27:01.870
We're going to stay
with the crew.

438
00:27:02.410 --> 00:27:04.710
We've grown quite fond
of this ship.

439
00:27:04.710 --> 00:27:07.080
But we'll be waiting
for you, won't we?

440
00:27:12.720 --> 00:27:14.420
Do as you please!

441
00:27:14.420 --> 00:27:17.840
You're full-fledged
pirates now, after all.

442
00:27:17.840 --> 00:27:20.350
It's your choice to make!

443
00:27:25.600 --> 00:27:29.610
He's leaving, Pops!
Aren't you gonna send him off?

444
00:27:32.240 --> 00:27:35.070
Roger left behind all his
ship's cargo as a thank you!

445
00:27:35.070 --> 00:27:37.160
This stuff is worth a fortune!

446
00:27:37.160 --> 00:27:39.910
I've never seen so much food!

447
00:27:39.910 --> 00:27:43.410
What? Give it back, now!

448
00:27:43.410 --> 00:27:46.210
They need it more than
we do, you morons!

449
00:27:46.210 --> 00:27:49.080
Don't you dare let
Oden's family go hungry!

450
00:27:49.080 --> 00:27:51.460
Put that back on
their ship, immediately!

451
00:27:51.460 --> 00:27:53.300
I won't say it twice!

452
00:27:53.300 --> 00:27:54.340
Yessir!

453
00:27:54.340 --> 00:27:55.920
Right away!

454
00:28:00.430 --> 00:28:02.850
Goodbye, Lord Oden!

455
00:28:06.060 --> 00:28:11.060
Goodbye, everyone!
I'll be back!

456
00:28:12.320 --> 00:28:15.030
You better make
all of us proud, all right?

457
00:28:15.030 --> 00:28:19.530
Can't wait to hear the stories!
Have fun out there! See ya!

458
00:28:19.530 --> 00:28:21.950
Be safe, all of you!

459
00:28:32.930 --> 00:28:36.180
It was the second act
of my life as a pirate.

460
00:28:36.180 --> 00:28:38.850
A new adventure had begun!

461
00:28:38.850 --> 00:28:39.680
White-Kichi is a great man,
but Roger is remarkable, too!

462
00:28:39.680 --> 00:28:42.010
White-kichi is a great man.

463
00:28:42.010 --> 00:28:44.680
But Roger is remarkable, too!

464
00:28:45.220 --> 00:28:48.180
I'm lucky to have met them both!

465
00:28:51.730 --> 00:28:55.190
What a sweet
little pea you are!

466
00:28:55.570 --> 00:28:57.150
Whoopsie-doodle!

467
00:28:58.030 --> 00:29:00.910
I haven't held a baby
in a long time!

468
00:29:00.910 --> 00:29:04.080
Y'know, it reminds me
of the old days.

469
00:29:04.530 --> 00:29:07.660
Momonosuke. And Hiyori, huh?

470
00:29:10.880 --> 00:29:15.090
Ah, big smiles!
That's my girl!

471
00:29:20.050 --> 00:29:23.770
Captain Roger, sir!
We got a stowaway!

472
00:29:31.610 --> 00:29:32.680
Viper!

473
00:29:34.650 --> 00:29:36.400
Why are you here?

474
00:29:36.400 --> 00:29:37.770
Well, why not?

475
00:29:37.770 --> 00:29:39.110
We figured we'd have more fun

476
00:29:39.110 --> 00:29:41.270
being with you-gara
on your travels!

477
00:29:41.270 --> 00:29:44.150
The dog
and the cat have disappeared!

478
00:29:45.320 --> 00:29:48.820
Dammit! Those two!

479
00:29:51.680 --> 00:29:53.370
Listen. The only reason
you're here is

480
00:29:53.370 --> 00:29:56.540
because you can decipher
those Poneglyphs.

481
00:29:56.540 --> 00:29:59.050
Nothing more, understand?

482
00:29:59.900 --> 00:30:02.610
<b>Mock Town, Jaya</b>

483
00:30:02.860 --> 00:30:05.230
Next up, I need radishes!

484
00:30:05.230 --> 00:30:07.040
Thief! Get back here!

485
00:30:07.040 --> 00:30:09.540
Oh, Captain's gonna
kick his butt.

486
00:30:11.540 --> 00:30:14.590
Oden!
Don't mess with the locals!

487
00:30:14.590 --> 00:30:17.050
I need to get more ingredients!

488
00:30:17.050 --> 00:30:18.590
Just what do you need them for?

489
00:30:24.870 --> 00:30:27.410
Y'see the balls on this guy?

490
00:30:30.160 --> 00:30:33.540
Wait, are we in a lawless land?

491
00:30:33.540 --> 00:30:35.130
Are you seeing this, Gaban?

492
00:30:35.130 --> 00:30:39.260
I am. So, they aren't
civilians after all.

493
00:31:13.300 --> 00:31:15.260
Holy crap! Badass!

494
00:31:15.260 --> 00:31:19.510
You're okay!
That was awesome!

495
00:31:20.350 --> 00:31:24.520
So. I guess since
they're not civilians.

496
00:31:24.520 --> 00:31:29.560
They're fair game.
Are you ready?

497
00:31:29.560 --> 00:31:31.230
Indeed!

498
00:31:33.360 --> 00:31:36.240
I still
need some kelp!

499
00:31:36.240 --> 00:31:37.620
What's it for?

500
00:31:37.620 --> 00:31:40.910
To make a delicious broth.

501
00:31:44.960 --> 00:31:46.250
You're a weirdo.

502
00:31:47.330 --> 00:31:50.090
All right. Enough of that.

503
00:31:50.090 --> 00:31:51.420
Mess these guys up!

504
00:32:31.960 --> 00:32:33.460
Are you not feeling well?

505
00:32:33.460 --> 00:32:36.170
I'm fine.
Nothing to worry about!

506
00:32:36.170 --> 00:32:38.380
What do you mean,
"nothing to worry about"?

507
00:32:38.380 --> 00:32:41.140
Best case scenario,
he's got a year or so to live.

508
00:32:44.220 --> 00:32:47.720
Gotta catch the wind
in my sails. While I can.

509
00:32:51.620 --> 00:32:52.870
Here goes! That's the
Knock Up Stream ahead!

510
00:32:52.870 --> 00:32:54.820
the Log Pose
suddenly pointing up?

511
00:33:04.300 --> 00:33:06.590
We're dead!

512
00:33:23.280 --> 00:33:24.610
An island?

513
00:33:27.610 --> 00:33:28.990
No way!

514
00:33:33.790 --> 00:33:35.540
The Sky Island!

515
00:33:35.540 --> 00:33:38.330
We gladly welcome you,
people from the Blue Sea!

516
00:33:43.920 --> 00:33:47.460
The world is so much
vaster than I had imagined!

517
00:33:47.460 --> 00:33:49.140
Not even the gods
could have predicted

518
00:33:49.140 --> 00:33:51.340
people living in the clouds!

519
00:34:00.270 --> 00:34:01.400
That fool.

520
00:34:01.400 --> 00:34:04.230
It takes ten years
to master a waver!

521
00:34:12.490 --> 00:34:13.830
Run for your lives!

522
00:34:26.050 --> 00:34:28.090
This is it! The City of Gold.

523
00:34:28.090 --> 00:34:29.300
Shandora!

524
00:34:29.300 --> 00:34:31.370
– Wow!
– Wow!

525
00:34:31.370 --> 00:34:33.420
I found it!

526
00:34:33.420 --> 00:34:33.720
All the way up here?!

527
00:34:33.720 --> 00:34:35.220
All the way up here?

528
00:34:41.420 --> 00:34:45.010
That must be it!
Shandora's grand belfry!

529
00:34:45.010 --> 00:34:46.850
That thing's pure gold!

530
00:34:46.850 --> 00:34:48.510
How do we haul it back, Captain?

531
00:34:48.510 --> 00:34:50.220
No time for that.

532
00:34:50.220 --> 00:34:51.980
Tell you what:
you can come get it

533
00:34:51.980 --> 00:34:53.560
when you're a captain yourself.

534
00:34:53.560 --> 00:34:55.100
Sound good, Buggy?

535
00:34:55.100 --> 00:34:58.230
Aww! Can't we break off
a little piece, at least?

536
00:34:58.230 --> 00:35:00.690
The voices echoing
within this stone are strong,

537
00:35:00.690 --> 00:35:02.570
so it was easy to find!

538
00:35:02.570 --> 00:35:05.700
It's speaking of
a great power, isn't it?

539
00:35:14.500 --> 00:35:17.670
The inscription tells of
a weapon named Poseidon.

540
00:35:17.670 --> 00:35:19.170
Interesting.

541
00:35:20.500 --> 00:35:24.220
Oden. You're able to write in
this script as well, aren't you?

542
00:35:24.220 --> 00:35:27.050
Yes. Of course!

543
00:35:27.050 --> 00:35:28.800
Carve this message!

544
00:35:37.560 --> 00:35:39.270
It's hard to believe Roger is

545
00:35:39.270 --> 00:35:40.860
nearing the end of his life.

546
00:35:40.860 --> 00:35:43.690
He carries on this quest
with such urgency.

547
00:35:43.690 --> 00:35:46.530
I must help him see it
to its conclusion.

548
00:35:48.320 --> 00:35:50.830
Like this, Captain?

549
00:35:50.830 --> 00:35:53.060
That should do it. Nice work!

550
00:35:53.060 --> 00:35:53.200
I made it here, and I will
guide this passage

551
00:35:53.200 --> 00:35:55.560
I made it here,
and I will guide this passage

552
00:35:55.560 --> 00:35:58.210
all the way to the farthest
ends of the world.

553
00:35:58.210 --> 00:36:01.190
The stormiest seas
will not stop me.

554
00:36:11.810 --> 00:36:14.180
I must see it, Roger.

555
00:36:14.180 --> 00:36:16.530
Show me the final chapter
of the adventure

556
00:36:16.530 --> 00:36:19.400
you've devoted your life to!

557
00:36:26.740 --> 00:36:29.740
Well, boys.
Let's go back to the Blue Sea!
